    "https://nwmissouri.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Northwest-Missouri-State-University-Maryville/Assistant-Professor-of-Biology_R-00201": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSALARY: $57,135.00 POSITION TITLE: Assistant Professor of Biology DEPARTMENT : Biology JOB DESCRIPTION: EMPLOYMENT TERMS: Tenure Track, Full-time, 9-month contract PRIMARY DUTY: Seeking a plant ecologist with a background in plant diversity, taxonomy, and local flora to teach undergraduate coursework in plant biology as well as advanced courses dealing with plant diversity.  Teaching responsibilities are likely to include an introductory course in organismal diversity and ecology as well as upper-level courses in field botany and plant biology.  The ability to contribute to the curriculum by offering courses in evolution, plant anatomy, plant physiology or other areas of the candidate’s specialization are highly desirable ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Teach an introductory survey (100 level) of organismal diversity and ecology for biology majors, including an associated laboratory component. Teach an upper-level field course focusing upon Local Flora of the region. Teach an upper-level course in plant biology and associated laboratory. Contribute to the biology discipline curriculum in other ways by offering courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Possibilities may include, but are not limited to, coursework in evolution, plant physiology, and plant anatomy.  Alternatively, the candidate may be asked to contribute to offerings of the biology survey for non-science majors as a part of the general education curriculum. Cover a typical annual teaching load of 12 load hours per term (fall and spring). Develop scholarly activity that involves undergraduate and/or master’s students. Manage the departmental greenhouse and herbarium. Serve the School and University on committees as assigned. Provide additional student support in the form of academic advisement, mentorship, or other student assistance as appropriate. Hold seven office hours/week. Other duties assigned by the Chair. REQUIREMENTS: Education: Ph.D. in biology or related scientific discipline.  ABD candidates will be considered. Skills: Good classroom management and lecture skills. WORKING CONDITIONS: Typical university classroom, office, laboratory, and field conditions.      EQUIPMENT/MATERIALS USED: Common classroom teaching equipment, laboratory instrumentation, and equipment for field studies.               TYPICAL PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Ability to complete essential functions in the classroom, laboratory, and field. COMMUNITY: Northwest Missouri State University located in Maryville, Missouri, a community of 12,000 with a diverse economy and a strong industrial base. Maryville is located 45 miles north of St. Joseph, Missouri, 90 miles north of Kansas City, Missouri, and 110 miles southeast of Omaha, Nebraska. For more information visit the city’s website at www.maryville.org . UNIVERSITY: With an enrollment of more than 8,500 students, Northwest is a coeducational, primarily residential four-year university that offers a broad range of undergraduate and selected graduate programs on its Maryville campus and through Northwest Online .   Founded in 1905, Northwest boasts a high retention rate and a graduation rate in the 95th percentile among its peers. Additionally, results of the Ruffalo Noel Levitz Student Satisfaction Inventory show Northwest students are more satisfied than students at national peers, and 78 percent of Northwest students report they would repeat their university experience, compared to 75 percent of students surveyed nationally at their respective institutions.   Furthermore, the University is a national model for student success and career placement with 93 percent of bachelor’s degree earners and 98 percent of master’s degree earners securing employment or continuing their education within six months of completing a degree at Northwest, according to the most recent data .    Northwest places a high emphasis on profession-based learning to help graduates get a jumpstart on their careers while maintaining competitive tuition rates and generous financial assistance to help minimize the financial barriers students may face when pursuing a college degree.   Students have opportunities to build their résumés with experiences on campus in nearly every area of study, including the  Horace Mann Laboratory School ,  National Public Radio affiliate KXCV , the R.T. Wright Farm ,  Mozingo Outdoor Education Recreation Area ,  a partnership with the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency or  Knacktive , a student-driven integrated digital marketing communications agency. In conjunction with its emergency and disaster management program, Northwest organizes and hosts Missouri Hope , an annual mass casualty training exercise that attracts first responders and emergency workers from throughout the nation and provides hands-on training in preparation for a natural disaster.   The University’s vibrant and diverse learning community also offers more than 150 student organizations, and  textbooks and a laptop are included  in tuition, saving students an estimated $6,900 over four years. Northwest offers 1,200 student employment positions, allowing students to build professional skills through its internationally benchmarked student employment program.    For more information about Northwest and its performance, visit  www.nwmissouri.edu/aboutus/facts/ ."
    },
    "https://nwmissouri.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Northwest-Missouri-State-University-Maryville/Assistant-Professor-of-Biology_R-00200": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSALARY: $57,135.00 POSITION TITLE: Assistant Professor of Biology DEPARTMENT : Biology JOB DESCRIPTION: EMPLOYMENT TERMS: Tenure Track, Full-time, 9-month contract PRIMARY DUTY: Seeking a biologist to offer various courses for biology majors and students preparing for admission to professional programs in health care fields.  A background and ability to offer an upper-level course in human or animal physiology for biology majors is essential.  Additional teaching assignments are likely to include a physiology course for nursing and allied health students and contributions to the introductory biology sequence for science majors.  Additional assignments may include medical terminology and other courses suited to the applicant’s area of expertise.(12-hour load per semester) ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Teach an upper level course in Human Physiology suitable for biology majors. Teach a 200 level physiology course for students in nursing and other allied health fields. Teach in the introductory sequence biology sequence for science majors, either an introduction to cells and molecular biology or a course in biological diversity, currently in development. Contribute to the biology discipline curriculum in other ways by offering courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Offerings related to neurophysiology and cancer biology are attractive but we are open to a wide range of possibilities. Cover a typical annual teaching load of 12 load hours per term (fall and spring). Develop scholarly activity that involves undergraduate and/or master’s students. Serve the School and University on committees as assigned. Provide additional student support in the form of academic advisement, mentorship, or other student assistance as appropriate. Hold seven office hours/week. Other duties as assigned by the Chair. REQUIREMENTS: Education: Ph.D. in biology or related scientific discipline.  ABD candidates will be considered. Skills: Good classroom management and lecture skills. WORKING CONDITIONS: Typical university classroom, office, laboratory, and field conditions.      EQUIPMENT/MATERIALS USED: Common classroom teaching equipment, laboratory instrumentation, and equipment for field studies.               TYPICAL PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Ability to complete essential functions in the classroom, laboratory, and field. COMMUNITY: Northwest Missouri State University located in Maryville, Missouri, a community of 12,000 with a diverse economy and a strong industrial base. Maryville is located 45 miles north of St. Joseph, Missouri, 90 miles north of Kansas City, Missouri, and 110 miles southeast of Omaha, Nebraska. For more information visit the city’s website at www.maryville.org . UNIVERSITY: With an enrollment of more than 8,500 students, Northwest is a coeducational, primarily residential four-year university that offers a broad range of undergraduate and selected graduate programs on its Maryville campus and through Northwest Online .   Founded in 1905, Northwest boasts a high retention rate and a graduation rate in the 95th percentile among its peers. Additionally, results of the Ruffalo Noel Levitz Student Satisfaction Inventory show Northwest students are more satisfied than students at national peers, and 78 percent of Northwest students report they would repeat their university experience, compared to 75 percent of students surveyed nationally at their respective institutions.   Furthermore, the University is a national model for student success and career placement with 93 percent of bachelor’s degree earners and 98 percent of master’s degree earners securing employment or continuing their education within six months of completing a degree at Northwest, according to the most recent data .    Northwest places a high emphasis on profession-based learning to help graduates get a jumpstart on their careers while maintaining competitive tuition rates and generous financial assistance to help minimize the financial barriers students may face when pursuing a college degree.   Students have opportunities to build their résumés with experiences on campus in nearly every area of study, including the  Horace Mann Laboratory School ,  National Public Radio affiliate KXCV , the R.T. Wright Farm ,  Mozingo Outdoor Education Recreation Area ,  a partnership with the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency or  Knacktive , a student-driven integrated digital marketing communications agency. In conjunction with its emergency and disaster management program, Northwest organizes and hosts Missouri Hope , an annual mass casualty training exercise that attracts first responders and emergency workers from throughout the nation and provides hands-on training in preparation for a natural disaster.   The University’s vibrant and diverse learning community also offers more than 150 student organizations, and  textbooks and a laptop are included  in tuition, saving students an estimated $6,900 over four years. Northwest offers 1,200 student employment positions, allowing students to build professional skills through its internationally benchmarked student employment program.    For more information about Northwest and its performance, visit  www.nwmissouri.edu/aboutus/facts/ ."
    },
    "https://nwmissouri.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Northwest-Missouri-State-University-Maryville/Financial-Assistance-Counselor_R-00173": {
      "title": "Financial Assistance Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSALARY: $19.35 POSITION TITLE: Financial Assistance Counselor DEPARTMENT : Financial Assistance Counseling and Outreach JOB DESCRIPTION: Salary Range: $19.35 - $21.50 PRIMARY DUTY: The Financial Assistance Counselor is primarily responsible for providing advice and counsel to students, families, and the campus community, while administering designated programs and executing procedures in the Office of Scholarships and Financial Assistance. Secondary responsibility is for program coordination, processing, and oversight. A Counselor is expected to develop and maintain a thorough understanding of guidance governing Federal, state, and institutional financial assistance programs. The position requires the Counselor to work in a team environment to coordinate efforts in administering designated programs and educating/training other staff regarding designated programs. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Service-related functions Provide advice and counsel to students, families, and the campus community, either in-person, by phone, or through written correspondence, including email. Utilize available resources to provide information in group and one-on-one settings. Serve as liaison for other University departments and various related off-campus agencies Develop and maintain a thorough understanding of guidance governing Federal, state, and institutional financial assistance programs. Exercise professional judgement when appropriate and Federal, state, or institutional guidelines do not seem to adequately address a particular situation. Keep updated on financial assistance trends. Monitor updates and changes with Banner student information system. Perform other duties as assigned Process-related functions Responsible for administration of designated programs and execution of procedures within the Office Scholarship and Financial Assistance. Coordinate efforts required to administer designated programs and educate/train other staff regarding designated programs. Perform other duties as assigned Requirements: Education: Requires high school diploma or equivalent and some coursework toward bachelor’s degree. Experience: Two years related customer service or financial guidance experience (Bachelor’s degree considered in lieu of experience). Skills: Strong interpersonal and group communications skills, ability to multi-task and work closely with others, strong information technology skills. WORKING CONDITIONS: This position will work in an office environment from the hours of 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. with a one-hour lunch break. This position will also require occasional evening and weekend hours. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: Limited supervision of student employees EQUIPMENT/MATERIALS USED: Typical office equipment TYPICAL PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Ability to lift up to 20 pounds COMMUNITY: Northwest Missouri State University located in Maryville, Missouri, a community of 12,000 with a diverse economy and a strong industrial base. Maryville is located 45 miles north of St. Joseph, Missouri, 90 miles north of Kansas City, Missouri, and 110 miles southeast of Omaha, Nebraska. For more information visit the city’s website at www.maryville.org . UNIVERSITY: With an enrollment of more than 8,500 students, Northwest is a coeducational, primarily residential four-year university that offers a broad range of undergraduate and selected graduate programs on its Maryville campus and through Northwest Online .   Founded in 1905, Northwest boasts a high retention rate and a graduation rate in the 95th percentile among its peers. Additionally, results of the Ruffalo Noel Levitz Student Satisfaction Inventory show Northwest students are more satisfied than students at national peers, and 78 percent of Northwest students report they would repeat their university experience, compared to 75 percent of students surveyed nationally at their respective institutions.   Furthermore, the University is a national model for student success and career placement with 93 percent of bachelor’s degree earners and 98 percent of master’s degree earners securing employment or continuing their education within six months of completing a degree at Northwest, according to the most recent data .    Northwest places a high emphasis on profession-based learning to help graduates get a jumpstart on their careers while maintaining competitive tuition rates and generous financial assistance to help minimize the financial barriers students may face when pursuing a college degree.   Students have opportunities to build their résumés with experiences on campus in nearly every area of study, including the  Horace Mann Laboratory School ,  National Public Radio affiliate KXCV , the R.T. Wright Farm ,  Mozingo Outdoor Education Recreation Area ,  a partnership with the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency or  Knacktive , a student-driven integrated digital marketing communications agency. In conjunction with its emergency and disaster management program, Northwest organizes and hosts Missouri Hope , an annual mass casualty training exercise that attracts first responders and emergency workers from throughout the nation and provides hands-on training in preparation for a natural disaster.   The University’s vibrant and diverse learning community also offers more than 150 student organizations, and  textbooks and a laptop are included  in tuition, saving students an estimated $6,900 over four years. Northwest offers 1,200 student employment positions, allowing students to build professional skills through its internationally benchmarked student employment program.    For more information about Northwest and its performance, visit  www.nwmissouri.edu/aboutus/facts/ ."
